From 00483615ff30d226da271dada0d72d37f00276d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini experiment archive <experiment@invalid.example>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 11:22:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wlan: join native firmware payload digests to DMA transfers

Carry a borrowed synchronous chunk witness from the divided-image loop
through command allocation, NIC staging and the actual AHB DMA port call.
Require the image owner and exact source, command and coalescing-buffer
extents. Hash only the bounded payload before DMA_TO_DEVICE mapping,
using the image's existing generic SHA-256 transform.

Record each chunk digest, DMA ordinal and native port return. Require all
eight chunk lifetimes before successful image observation. Refuse capture
for PIO, alternate mapping, missing stages or native failure without
changing native transfers, polling, cleanup, allocation or return values.
Keep existing no-witness entry points and the original HAL macro path.

This unselected experiment does not prove post-hash buffer immutability,
firmware execution or resource isolation. Added lock duration, complete
linking, controller integration and device admission remain open. The
synthetic archive author supplies no DCO certification.
